1
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:05,599
Chapter 6. The street.

2
00:00:05,600 --> 00:00:09,759
If I had been astonished at first catching a glimpse of so outlandish an

3
00:00:09,760 --> 00:00:15,278
individual as Quiquake circulating among the polite society of a civilized town,

4
00:00:15,279 --> 00:00:19,599
that astonishment soon departed upon taking my first daylight stroll through

5
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:24,959
the streets of New Bedford. In thorough affairs nei the docks any considerable

6
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:28,959
seapport will frequently offer to view the queerest looking nond-escripts from

7
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:34,078
foreign parts. Even in Broadway and chestnut streets Mediterranean mariners

8
00:00:34,079 --> 00:00:38,959
will sometimes jostle the afrighted ladies. Regent street is not unknown to

9
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:45,278
lascars and melees. And at Bombay in the Apollo green live Yankees have often

10
00:00:45,279 --> 00:00:50,559
scared the natives. But New Bedford beats all Water Street in whopping. In

11
00:00:50,560 --> 00:00:55,519
these last mentioned haunts you see only sailors, but in New Bedford actual

12
00:00:55,520 --> 00:01:00,559
cannibals stand chatting at street corners, savages outright, many of whom

13
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:03,759
yet carry on their bones unholy flesh.

14
00:01:03,760 --> 00:01:06,799
It makes a stranger stare.

15
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:14,879
But besides the Fijians, Tonga Deborars, Aromangoans, Panangians, and Brigians, and besides

16
00:01:14,880 --> 00:01:19,519
the wild specimens of the whailing craft, which unheated reel about the

17
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:25,117
streets, you will see other sites still more curious, certainly more comical.

18
00:01:25,118 --> 00:01:30,718
Their weekly arrive in this town, scores of green verters and New Hampshiremen,

19
00:01:30,719 --> 00:01:35,358
all a thirst for gain and glory in the fishery. They are mostly young, of

20
00:01:35,359 --> 00:01:40,237
stalwart frames, fellows who have felled forests, and now seek to drop the axe

21
00:01:40,238 --> 00:01:45,197
and snatch the whale lance. Many are as green as the green mountains whence they

22
00:01:45,198 --> 00:01:50,237
came. In some things you would think them but a few hours old. Look there,

23
00:01:50,238 --> 00:01:54,879
that chap struting around the corner. He wears a beaver hat and swallowtailed

24
00:01:54,880 --> 00:01:59,599
coat, girdled with a sailor belt and sheath knife. Here comes another with a

25
00:01:59,600 --> 00:02:02,799
southwester and a bombazine cloak.

26
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:07,358
No town bred dandy will compare with a country bred one. I mean a downright

27
00:02:07,359 --> 00:02:12,879
bumpkin dandy. A fellow that in the dog days will mow his two acres in buckskin

28
00:02:12,880 --> 00:02:15,519
gloves for fear of tanning his hands.

29
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:19,759
Now when a country dandy like this takes it into his head to make a distinguished

30
00:02:19,760 --> 00:02:24,478
reputation and joins the great whale fishery, you should see the comical

31
00:02:24,479 --> 00:02:29,038
things he does upon reaching the seapport. In bespeaking his sea outfit,

32
00:02:29,039 --> 00:02:34,237
he orders bell buttons to his waist coats, straps to his canvas trousers.

33
00:02:34,238 --> 00:02:38,959
Ah, poor hay seed, how bitterly will burst those straps in the first howling

34
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:44,237
gale when thou art driven straps button and all down the throat of the tempest.

35
00:02:44,238 --> 00:02:49,197
But think not that this famous town has only harpooners, cannibals, and bumpkins

36
00:02:49,198 --> 00:02:55,197
to show her visitors. Not at all. Still New Bedford is a queer place. Had it not

37
00:02:55,198 --> 00:02:59,919
been for us whalemen, that tract of land would this day perhaps have been in as

38
00:02:59,920 --> 00:03:04,559
howling condition as the coast of Labrador, as it is, parts of her back

39
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:09,438
country are enough to frighten one. They look so bony. The town itself is perhaps

40
00:03:09,439 --> 00:03:13,839
the dearest place to live in in all New England. It is a land of oil, true

41
00:03:13,840 --> 00:03:19,839
enough, but not like Canaan, a land also of corn and wine. The streets do not run

42
00:03:19,840 --> 00:03:25,038
with milk, nor in the springtime do they pave them with fresh eggs. Yet in spite

43
00:03:25,039 --> 00:03:30,478
of this, nowhere in all America will you find more patrician-like houses, parks,

44
00:03:30,479 --> 00:03:35,839
and gardens more opulent than in New Bedford. Whence came they how planted

45
00:03:35,840 --> 00:03:41,358
upon this once scraggy skoria of a country. Go and gaze upon the iron

46
00:03:41,359 --> 00:03:45,759
emblematical harpoons round yonder lofty mansion, and your question will be

47
00:03:45,760 --> 00:03:50,318
answered. Yes, all these brave houses and flowery gardens came from the

48
00:03:50,319 --> 00:03:55,678
Atlantic, Pacific, and Indian Ocean. One and all they were harpooned and dragged

49
00:03:55,679 --> 00:03:58,078
up hither from the bottom of the sea.

50
00:03:58,079 --> 00:04:04,157
Can her Alexander perform a feat like that? In New Bedford, fathers, they say,

51
00:04:04,158 --> 00:04:08,638
give whales for the for dowers to their daughters and portion off their nieces

52
00:04:08,639 --> 00:04:13,278
with a few porpuses a piece. You must go to New Bedford to see a brilliant

53
00:04:13,279 --> 00:04:17,438
wedding, for they say they have reservoirs of oil in every house, and

54
00:04:17,439 --> 00:04:22,318
every night recklessly burn their lengths in spermicetti candles. In

55
00:04:22,319 --> 00:04:27,759
summertime the town is sweet to see, full of fine maples, long avenues of

56
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:33,117
green and gold. And in August, high in air, the beautiful and bountiful horse

57
00:04:33,118 --> 00:04:38,237
chestnuts candalabra wise profer the passer by their tapering upright cones

58
00:04:38,238 --> 00:04:40,638
of congregated blossoms.

59
00:04:40,639 --> 00:04:45,919
So omnipotent is art, which in many a district of New Bedford has superinduced

60
00:04:45,920 --> 00:04:50,799
bright terraces of flowers upon the barren refuge rocks thrown aside at

61
00:04:50,800 --> 00:04:56,638
creation's final day. And the women of New Bedford, they bloom like their own

62
00:04:56,639 --> 00:05:02,157
red roses, but roses only bloom in summer, whereas the fine carnation of

63
00:05:02,158 --> 00:05:07,117
their cheeks is perennial as sunlight in the seventh heavens. Elsewhere match

64
00:05:07,118 --> 00:05:13,117
that bloom of theirs you cannot save in Salem where they tell me the young girls

65
00:05:13,118 --> 00:05:18,398
breathe such musk their sailor sweethearts smell them miles offshore as

66
00:05:18,399 --> 00:05:26,039
though they were drawing nigh the odorous malucas instead of the puritanic sands
